"none\" stroke=\"#F2E3C9\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n <circle r=\"97\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#6E7E78\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n <g><animateTransform .../><use href=\"#spokes\"/></g>\n</g>\n```\nTire outer 13 means outer radius 106.5? stroke centered on r=100, outer 106.5, bottom y=584.5 if center 478. Then ground at 584. So shadow center 586. Let's set wheel center 478, r=96, tire stroke 13 -> outer 102.5, bottom 580.5. Good. rim 88. Use spokes ±84. Let's set wheel r=96, spokes radius 85, rim 88. Tire bottom 580.5. Ground line 580. Great.\n\nCenters rear (290,478), front (695,478), r=96. Bottom = 580.5. Shadow y=584.\n\nFrame geometry use front hub 695,478.\n\nSpokes + rim:\n- tire circle r=96 stroke 13\n- inner rim circle r=86 stroke 4 pale\n- accent circle r=91 stroke teal 2 opacity .35 maybe.\n- rotating spokes ±82.\nHub.\nFenders maybe no.\n\nFrame:\n- rear hub\n- BB\n- seat cluster 438,375\n- head top 652,338\n- head bottom 668,398\n- front hub\nPaths:\nchainstay M290 478 L488 487\nseatstay M290 478 L438 375\nseat tube M488 487 L438 375\ntop tube M438 375 L652 338\ndown tube M488 487 L668 398\nhead tube M652 338 L668 398\nfork M668 398 C674 425 686 453 695 478\nseatpost M438 374 L430 362\nmaybe small rear dropout.\nOutline width 13, inner 7.5. Fork inner 6.5. Head tube maybe thicker.\nMaybe top tube has slight curve. straight okay.\n\nAdd chain:\n`M290 467 L488 455 A32 32 0 0 1 488 519 L290 489 A11 11 0 0 1 290 467Z`\nstroke #2A3432 width 4.5 fill none dasharray `5 4` animate dashoffset -18. Add top chain highlight #72817? maybe not. Draw before frame? chain should be visible behind chainring but could be behind chainstay. Draw after wheels before frame then chainring. Fine.\n\nCrank near draw after frame and chain:\nChainring outer teeth circle r=33 stroke width 7 dasharray 4 4; face r=28 fill #C8B08A stroke dark 3; inner ring r=18 etc. Add holes 6 at radius 22 r=3, fill maybe background teal/dark #42514D. Center r=8.\nCrank arm near from 0 to 36. Stroke 10 dark with inner steel 5? Draw path dark 11, path silver 4.5, or dark arm with highlight line offset. Use dark ink line width 10, inner `#B9A37F` width 4. It looks metallic. Add cream highlight.\nPedal group.\n\nFar crank behind frame:\nFar arm from 0 to -36 dark; far pedal rectangle. Foot far drawn after? Far foot should be near pedal. We draw far crank group and far leg group; both before frame. That works. But foot far should be above far pedal. Draw far crank, then far leg/foot. However far leg upper also behind frame. Good.\nLayer order:\nwheels, chain? chain behind frame; far crank; far leg/foot; chain; frame; saddle? near crank; near leg; bird.\nBut far leg should maybe be in front of chain? fine.\nSaddle after frame and near crank? saddle above frame. Near leg after saddle. okay.\nHandlebar after frame before bird. Saddle before body.\nDust puffs behind wheel maybe before wheels.\n\nOrder plan:\nbg\nshadow\nspeed lines\nfar crank + far leg\nwheels\nchain\nframe\nheadset/handlebar/saddle\nnear crank\nnear leg\nbird tail/neck/body/wing/head/beak/scarf\ndust maybe foreground at bottom\nMaybe wheels should be behind frame yes. Far crank behind frame, but if drawn before wheels, far arm could be hidden by wheel? It is around BB x452..524, y487, not overlapping wheels much. Behind near wheel? no. Draw far crank before wheels to avoid on top; foot emerges. Actually far crank/foot at BB and can overlap rear wheel rim near x452? rear wheel extends to x386, so no. Front wheel from x599, so no. Good. Draw wheels then far crank/far leg? Far leg behind frame but in front of wheels if it overlaps. Better draw wheels first, then far crank/far leg. Both behind frame. Fine.\n\nNear chainring overlaps frame; draw after frame.\nSaddle etc.\n\nSaddle:\n```\n<g id=\"saddle\">\n <path d=\"M438 374 L430 362\" stroke outline.../>\n <path d=\"M381 367 C398 360 436 360 470 366 C479 368 479 375 470 377 C448 381 405 382 383 377 C375 375 375 370 381 367Z\" fill=\"#7A4B36\" stroke=\"#263436\" width=3.5/>\n <path d=\"M389 368 C406 364 438 364 465 368\" stroke=\"#A87455\" width=2 fill=none opacity=.7/>\n <circle cx=389 cy=371 r=2 fill=\"#E8C98F\"/>\n <circle cx=463 cy=371 r=2 fill.../>\n</g>\n```\nSaddle nose to right x479. Bird bottom around 362, should sit on it. Seat cluster 438,375. Good. But saddle y367 maybe sits above seat cluster. Fine.\nSeat post drawn in frame path from 438,375 to 430,362; saddle overlaps. Good.\n\nHandlebar:\nstem path M652 338 L655 315; bar path M636 314 C655 301 678 300 700 310; grip M687 306 L702 311 stroke brown width 13 rounded; maybe bar outline dark width 8 and inner teal 4.5. Use two paths.\nBrake lever from 682 306 C686 315 686 321 681 326.\nBell small at 652,302: circle.\nMaybe front lamp at (674,372) circle.\n\nFrame decorative: head badge small cream circle at (660,365). Maybe.\n\nBird layering carefully.\n\nLet's construct body, neck, tail.\n\nTail path define with animateTransform:\n```\n<g>\n <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"-1.5 330 330;1.5 330 330;-1.5 330 330\" dur=\"2.8s\" repeatCount=indefinite/>\n <path d=\"M332 315 C310 301 284 304 265 317 C284 320 296 327 304 336 C286 337 273 345 268 356 C290 351 313 359 333 349 C324 340 327 328 332 315Z\".../>\n <path d... feather lines/>\n</g>\n```\nMaybe tail should not animate dramatically; okay.\n\nBody:\n```\n<path d=\"M330 309 C306 303 287 313 277 327 C294 324 301 332 316 339 C328 352 354 362 390 362 C436 362 475 343 491 314 C506 289 505 258 489 235 C472 211 443 200 413 206 C378 213 351 233 339 261 C330 282 337 298 330 309Z\" fill=\"#FCF8EE\" stroke=\"#263436\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n```\nNeed tail joins body at x330. Tail path ends at x333. Good.\n\nBody under-shadow:\n```\n<path d=\"M335 306 C351 329 371 344 402 348 C441 353 472 335 484 311 C479 337 451 358 411 361 C372 364 345 346 335 306Z\" fill=\"#E7DDCC\" opacity=\".8\"/>\n```\nChest highlight near right top: path fill `#FFFDF7` opacity .8.\n\nFeat