{"type":"thinking","text":"Initial render. Issues:\n- Pelican looks like large duck/goose but beak huge & pouch good. Body is huge, wing weird? Wing appears as long thin pointed arm toward handlebar. Wing shape maybe okay but lower wing feather lines look thin. The near leg looks like a thin orange curve from saddle to pedal; okay.\n- Wheel spokes static but will animate.\n- Bird position: saddle looks like under body; good.\n- Major problem: head/neck: body huge and neck merges. The beak appears detached? Actually okay. But pelican eye seems weird perhaps head too small. Cap is nice.\n- Scarf appears as two big red blades? The tail looks like a red ribbon but there is weird floating knot. It might be confused with wing. The scarf band red crossing near neck. Looks okay but maybe tails too long/straight and overlap wing.\n- Wings: The near wing reaches handlebar but looks like a thin arm with a triangular wing from shoulder; shape is weird. It seems the wing is very long pointed with cream fold. Maybe works.\n- Rear wheel center x290, front 695, bike geometry, but saddles at 425. Bird body covers saddle. Seat tube partially visible. Fine.\n- Big blank space at top left; composition maybe okay but could be more energetic.\n- Ground/hills maybe okay.\n- Legs: near leg is orange curving from below body to pedal. Far leg hidden? likely okay.\n- The pelican legs are orange but very thin. Could be thicker and more bird-like; perhaps knee not visible due curve. Need perhaps add webbed foot? Initial foot on right pedal maybe is hidden by chainring/crank? Wait near foot at 524,481 should be visible. In preview at crank area near bottom right, I see maybe orange foot? The near leg goes down to right pedal? The orange line curves to around x524,y481, but then appears to end behind chainring? There is an orange foot at x524,y481? Crank at 488,487 and near pedal at 524,487. Foot shape maybe hidden by chainring? Wait z-order: near leg after near crank; should show foot. At image, orange line from saddle goes down to 524,481; maybe webfoot tiny and blends. I can zoom.\n\n- The near leg appears to start from saddle/seat area, not body. It curves from under body near saddle to pedal, but very thin. Could make thicker.\n- Cranks: near chainring visible. Crank arm maybe extends right to pedal but from preview near x524,y487 there is a dark something maybe hidden by orange leg. The foot covers pedal? Foot shape is small, not obvious. Need zoom.\n\n- Overall style nice, but user asked \"pelican actively riding a bicycle\". The bird is sitting upright, but pedaling. Need perhaps legs clearly visible and more dynamic. Also huge beak.\n\nNeed inspect at 2x crop. Use rsvg-convert with viewBox? Could crop via ImageMagick not available. Python PIL maybe installed. Let's check."}
