517`, knee (519,435). Yes. Perfect. Add near knee positions:\n0: (506,414)\n1: (519,435)\n2: (498,422)\n3: (513,406)\nFar knee positions:\n0: (476,416)\n1: (491,400)\n2: (497,424)\n3: (510,441)\n\nAdd `g` knee group with animateTransform translate values and a circle and maybe a little feather tuft. Since near leg drawn after crank, knee should be after foot? Foot on pedal independent. Add after orange path but before foot? either. Near knee circles added within near leg group. Far knee within far leg group before frame.\nDraw knee as circle r=5 fill #F2A33A stroke dark 2.5. This creates a visible joint and makes leg read as leg. Maybe also a slightly larger thigh from hip to knee but same width; okay.\n\nCould add a \"heel\" or webbed foot. The foot shape looks like a leaf/wooden shoe. Maybe reshape to clearly show webbed toes. Let's design better. Current foot at high zoom: looks like a yellow mitten with two lines. We can make a three-toed webbed foot with lobes at front. Use a path with three rounded toe lobes:\n```\nM -7 -1\nC -4 -6 1 -7 6 -5\nC 9 -8 14 -8 17 -4\nC 21 -6 25 -4 26 0\nC 27 4 23 7 19 6\nC 17 9 12 9 9 6\nC 5 9 0 9 -3 6\nC -7 5 -9 1 -7 -1Z\n```\nThis has lumps but maybe looks like a cloud. Better draw foot with distinct toe shapes by combining ellipses? Could draw base webbed shape with 3 toe capsules and fill dark orange. Simpler, we can make foot as follows:\n- Heel/ankle centered at x0.\n- Webbing triangular fan from (-2,0) to (22,-3) to (25,3) to (20,7) to (12,5) to (4,8) etc.\n- Add toe tips circles? Maybe.\n\nFoot could be drawn with 3 toes pointing right and slightly fanning:\n```\n<path d=\"M-6 -1 C-2 -6 3 -8 8 -5 C11 -7 15 -7 18 -3 C22 -5 25 -2 25 2 C27 6 22 8 18 6 C17 10 11 10 8 7 C4 10 -1 9 -4 6 C-8 5 -9 1 -6 -1Z\" fill.../>\n<path d=\"M1 1 C7 0 13 0 18 2 M2 4 C8 3 13 4 17 5\" .../>\n```\nMight be okay. Current shape is visually acceptable. The important thing is leg+foot movement.\n\nAnother issue: The scarf looks like a giant red paper 