dal stroke? In side view, vertical bob can be twice per revolution, but 1.4s cycle 2px is okay. Better 0 -1.5 0 -1.5 0? Not important.\nAdd rotate slight? Could add a second nested group? no.\n\nIf body bobs, the wing tip moves at handlebar by 2px. Looks okay.\nBut the head group also rotates. Fine.\nThis adds animation.\n\nAlso add a little top tube shimmer? no.\n\nAdd wheel valve highlight; yes.\n\nImportant: The near wheel and front wheel spins same direction (clockwise) for moving right. Yes, clockwise.\n\nChain animation direction: stroke-dashoffset negative moves dashes forward? not critical.\n\nCrank direction: clockwise. Left pedal moving up? At 0 near right, then down. For forward pedaling (bike moving right), cranks rotate clockwise (right pedal goes down). yes.\n\nDust moves left, correct.\n\nCould animate road dashes moving left slightly to imply travel? The road line dashes could move slowly backwards. This would further convey motion, but bike is fixed and wheels spin, no need. Maybe animate road dash offset to left over 2s. Could be nice. Use `<animate attributeName=\"stroke-dashoffset\" from=\"0\" to=\"54\" dur=\"1.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/>` on dashes. But when road dashes move, the scene feels like camera following bike? In side-scroller, yes. However ground texture pebbles static. Fine. Might be overkill. Keep static.\n\nAdd wheels subtle bob? no.\n\nLet's add body bob and maybe refine scarf to include trailing underside knot tails. Also fix static preview of knee? no.\n\nBefore adding, think if the body bob could detach scarf from wing etc none.\n\nAdd:\n```\n<g>\n  <animateTransform ... values=\"0 0;0 -2;0 0;0 1;0 0\" dur=\"1.4s\".../>\n...\n</g>\n```\nGroup is `<g>` before tail feathers line. It already exists. Add animateTransform right after. Need no base transform; static preview initial 0, fine.\n\nMaybe animating 2px down at 75% phase means body dips when pedal up. Fine.\n\nCould also animate beak/pouch jiggle by adding another smal